        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="jLvaAgckw38uRxlf_2XB-14" parent="1" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="465" width="789.92" x="865.37" y="100" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="&lt;h3 class=&quot;c-article__sub-heading&quot; id=&quot;Sec7&quot; style=&quot;-webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, Roboto, Oxygen-Sans, Ubuntu, Cantarell, &amp;quot;Helvetica Neue&amp;quot;, sans-serif; letter-spacing: -0.0117156rem; line-height: 1.24; box-sizing: inherit; font-style: normal; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); margin: 24px 0px 8px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 22px; background-color: light-dark(rgb(255, 255, 255), rgb(18, 18, 18)); color: light-dark(rgb(34, 34, 34), rgb(208, 208, 208)); letter-spacing: -0.0117156rem;&quot;&gt;HEX improves prognosis prediction in early-stage lung cancer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;overflow-wrap: break-word; word-break: break-word; box-sizing: inherit; margin-bottom: 24px; margin-top: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 22px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;With the ability to generate spatial proteomics from standard H&amp;amp;E images, HEX enables biologically interpretable prediction of clinically relevant outcomes by adding a new layer of molecular insight. Although H&amp;amp;E provides detailed tissue morphology, virtual CODEX maps offer complementary information about spatially resolved protein expression. To integrate these distinct yet synergistic data types, we developed &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;multimodal integration via co-attention (MICA), a deep learning framework that fuses H&amp;amp;E and virtual CODEX data at an early stage&lt;/b&gt; (Supplementary Fig.&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a data-track=&quot;click&quot; data-track-label=&quot;link&quot; data-track-action=&quot;supplementary material anchor&quot; href=&quot;https://www.nature.com/articles/s41591-025-04060-4#MOESM1&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 400; vertical-align: baseline; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 102, 153); overflow-wrap: break-word; text-decoration: underline 0.0625rem; text-decoration-skip-ink: auto; word-break: break-word; box-sizing: inherit; text-underline-offset: 0.08em;&quot;&gt;5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;and&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a data-track=&quot;click&quot; data-track-label=&quot;link&quot; data-track-action=&quot;section anchor&quot; href=&quot;https://www.nature.com/articles/s41591-025-04060-4#Sec13&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 400; vertical-align: baseline; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 102, 153); overflow-wrap: break-word; text-decoration: underline 0.0625rem; text-decoration-skip-ink: auto; word-break: break-word; box-sizing: inherit; text-underline-offset: 0.08em;&quot;&gt;Methods&lt;/a&gt;). This approach explicitly models cross-modal interactions and spatial relationships, enhancing its ability to identify clinically relevant features predictive of patient outcomes.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" link="&lt;h3 class=&quot;c-article__sub-heading&quot; id=&quot;Sec7&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 400; -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, Roboto, Oxygen-Sans, Ubuntu, Cantarell, &amp;quot;Helvetica Neue&amp;quot;, sans-serif; letter-spacing: -0.0117156rem; font-size: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.24; box-sizing: inherit; font-style: normal; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); margin: 24px 0px 8px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;&quot;&gt;HEX improves prognosis prediction in early-stage lung cancer&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;overflow-wrap: break-word; word-break: break-word; box-sizing: inherit; margin-bottom: 24px; margin-top: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif; font-size: 18px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;&quot;&gt;With the ability to generate spatial proteomics from standard H&amp;amp;E images, HEX enables biologically interpretable prediction of clinically relevant outcomes by adding a new layer of molecular insight. Although H&amp;amp;E provides detailed tissue morphology, virtual CODEX maps offer complementary information about spatially resolved protein expression. To integrate these distinct yet synergistic data types, we developed multimodal integration via co-attention (MICA), a deep learning framework that fuses H&amp;amp;E and virtual CODEX data at an early stage (Supplementary Fig.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a data-track=&quot;click&quot; data-track-label=&quot;link&quot; data-track-action=&quot;supplementary material anchor&quot; href=&quot;https://www.nature.com/articles/s41591-025-04060-4#MOESM1&quot; style=&quot;vertical-align: baseline; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 102, 153); overflow-wrap: break-word; text-decoration: underline 0.0625rem; text-decoration-skip-ink: auto; word-break: break-word; box-sizing: inherit; text-underline-offset: 0.08em;&quot;&gt;5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;and&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a data-track=&quot;click&quot; data-track-label=&quot;link&quot; data-track-action=&quot;section anchor&quot; href=&quot;https://www.nature.com/articles/s41591-025-04060-4#Sec13&quot; style=&quot;vertical-align: baseline; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 102, 153); overflow-wrap: break-word; text-decoration: underline 0.0625rem; text-decoration-skip-ink: auto; word-break: break-word; box-sizing: inherit; text-underline-offset: 0.08em;&quot;&gt;Methods&lt;/a&gt;). This approach explicitly models cross-modal interactions and spatial relationships, enhancing its ability to identify clinically relevant features predictive of patient outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;" id="jLvaAgckw38uRxlf_2XB-16">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="200" width="780" x="1740" y="120" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
