        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f67gIQNVw1lp-HuG7de4-1" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; float: none; display: inline !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Spatial proteomics&lt;/b&gt; enables high-resolution mapping of protein expression and can transform our understanding of biology and disease. However, major challenges remain for &lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;clinical translation&lt;/b&gt;, including cost, complexity and scalability. Here we present &lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;H&amp;amp;E to protein expression (HEX)&lt;/b&gt;, an AI model designed to computationally generate &lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;spatial proteomics profiles from standard histopathology slides.&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(255, 255, 255), rgb(18, 18, 18)); color: light-dark(rgb(34, 34, 34), rgb(208, 208, 208)); font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;Trained and validated on 819,000 histopathology image tiles with matched protein expression from 382 tumor samples, HEX accurately predicts the expression of 40 biomarkers encompassing immune, structural and functional programs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(255, 255, 255), rgb(18, 18, 18)); color: light-dark(rgb(34, 34, 34), rgb(208, 208, 208)); font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;HEX demonstrates substantial performance gains over alternative methods for protein expression prediction from H&amp;amp;E images.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; float: none; display: inline !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; float: none; display: inline !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;We develop a &lt;b&gt;multimodal data integration approach&lt;/b&gt; that combines the original &lt;b&gt;H&amp;amp;E image&lt;/b&gt; and AI-derived virtual&lt;b&gt; spatial proteomics&lt;/b&gt; to enhance outcome prediction. Applied to six independent non-small-cell lung cancer cohorts totaling 2,298 patients, HEX-enabled multimodal integration improved prognostic accuracy by 22% and immunotherapy response prediction by 24–39% compared with conventional clinicopathological and molecular biomarkers. Biological interpretation revealed spatially organized tumor–immune niches predictive of therapeutic response, including the co-localization of T helper cells and cytotoxic T cells in responders, and immunosuppressive tumor-associated macrophage and neutrophil aggregates in non-responders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="355" width="810" x="40" y="60.38" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f67gIQNVw1lp-HuG7de4-6" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif; text-align: start; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;same tissue section for tumor samples from &lt;b&gt;ten &lt;/b&gt;patients with NSCLC&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="260" x="20" y="646" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="&lt;font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; float: none; display: inline !important;&quot;&gt;We assessed the model accuracy for protein expression on two independent datasets with CODEX and H&amp;amp;E-stained tissue sections for 372 tumor samples. To further evaluate HEX’s generalizability beyond NSCLC, we externally validated HEX on a pan-cancer dataset containing 57-plex CODEX and matched H&amp;amp;E images across 206 tumor samples from 34 tissue types&lt;/span&gt;&lt;sup style=&quot;vertical-align: baseline; line-height: 0; position: relative; top: -0.5em; box-sizing: inherit; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;a data-track=&quot;click&quot; data-track-action=&quot;reference anchor&quot; data-track-label=&quot;link&quot; data-test=&quot;citation-ref&quot; aria-label=&quot;Reference 11&quot; title=&quot;Schürch, C. M. et al. Coordinated cellular neighborhoods orchestrate antitumoral immunity at the colorectal cancer invasive front. Cell 182, 1341–1359.e19 (2020).&quot; href=&quot;https://www.nature.com/articles/s41591-025-04060-4#ref-CR11&quot; id=&quot;ref-link-section-d247844688e770&quot; style=&quot;vertical-align: baseline; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 102, 153); overflow-wrap: break-word; text-decoration: underline 0.0625rem; text-decoration-skip-ink: auto; word-break: break-word; box-sizing: inherit; text-underline-offset: 0.08em;&quot;&gt;11&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; float: none; display: inline !important;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" link="&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif; font-size: 18px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; display: inline !important; float: none;&quot;&gt;We assessed the model accuracy for protein expression on two independent datasets with CODEX and H&amp;amp;E-stained tissue sections for 372 tumor samples. To further evaluate HEX’s generalizability beyond NSCLC, we externally validated HEX on a pan-cancer dataset containing 57-plex CODEX and matched H&amp;amp;E images across 206 tumor samples from 34 tissue types&lt;/span&gt;&lt;sup style=&quot;vertical-align: baseline; font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 0; position: relative; top: -0.5em; box-sizing: inherit; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;a data-track=&quot;click&quot; data-track-action=&quot;reference anchor&quot; data-track-label=&quot;link&quot; data-test=&quot;citation-ref&quot; aria-label=&quot;Reference 11&quot; title=&quot;Schürch, C. M. et al. Coordinated cellular neighborhoods orchestrate antitumoral immunity at the colorectal cancer invasive front. Cell 182, 1341–1359.e19 (2020).&quot; href=&quot;https://www.nature.com/articles/s41591-025-04060-4#ref-CR11&quot; id=&quot;ref-link-section-d247844688e770&quot; style=&quot;vertical-align: baseline; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 102, 153); overflow-wrap: break-word; text-decoration: underline 0.0625rem; text-decoration-skip-ink: auto; word-break: break-word; box-sizing: inherit; text-underline-offset: 0.08em;&quot;&gt;11&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif; font-size: 18px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; display: inline !important; float: none;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;" id="f67gIQNVw1lp-HuG7de4-9">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="170" width="190" x="667" y="520" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="f67gIQNVw1lp-HuG7de4-10" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif; font-size: 18px; text-align: start; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;The clinical relevance of HEX was evaluated across five independent NSCLC cohorts with 2,150 patients and 12 other cancer types with 5,019 patients for prognosis prediction, as well as in a separate cohort of 148 patients treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) for response prediction. Inclusion and exclusion:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif; font-size: 18px; text-align: start; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;Extended Data Fig.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a data-track=&quot;click&quot; data-track-label=&quot;link&quot; data-track-action=&quot;figure anchor&quot; href=&quot;https://www.nature.com/articles/s41591-025-04060-4#Fig8&quot; style=&quot;vertical-align: baseline; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(0, 102, 153); overflow-wrap: break-word; text-decoration-thickness: 0.0625rem; text-decoration-skip-ink: auto; word-break: break-word; box-sizing: inherit; text-underline-offset: 0.08em; font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif; font-size: 18px; text-align: start;&quot;&gt;2&lt;/a&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="10" width="657.5" x="20" y="1388.85" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f67gIQNVw1lp-HuG7de4-12" parent="1" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="230" width="595.69" x="-810" y="775" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
